Hi Mike ,

Thanks for the prompt reply. Yes certainly, here's my code pretty much from the beginning -

# Map coords
xmn <- -5.3
xmx <- -2.6
ymn <- 51.4
ymx <- 53.4

# Temporal extent
st_time <- as.POSIXlt("2023-07-01 00:00", tz = "UTC")
en_time <- as.POSIXlt("2023-12-31 23:00", tz = "UTC")

# Set prefix and path
file_prefix <- "era5_WJD23"
file_path <- getwd()

# Build and send request
req <- build_era5_request(xmin = xmn, xmax = xmx,
                          ymin = ymn, ymax = ymx,
                          start_time = st_time,
                          end_time = en_time,
                          outfile_name = file_prefix)

request_era5(request = req, uid = uid, out_path = file_path)

# Desired temporal extent from nc file
dstart <- "01/07/2023"
dfinish <- "31/12/2023"

# Singular point analysed from nc file
loc <- c(-3.72, 52.26) # somewhere in the middle of map

# Run microclimate model
micro <- micro_era5(loc = loc, dstart = dstart, dfinish = dfinish, spatial = 'C:\\ERA5\\era5_WJD23')

# Run ectotherm model
ecto <- ectotherm(T_F_min = 30, T_F_max = 35, T_pref = 33, T_B_min = 20, T_RB_min = 10)

The code works fine for the above script, it's when I add the scenario change in the following code that the error occurs -

# Run microclimate model with scenario change (+2)
micro <- micro_era5(loc = loc, dstart = dstart, dfinish = dfinish, scenario = 2, spatial = 'C:\\ERA5\\era5_WJD23')

And the following error is produced when the ectotherm model is run -

> ecto <- ectotherm(T_F_min = 30, T_F_max = 35, T_pref = 33, T_B_min = 20, T_RB_min = 10) error: maxshades must be a vector with a length equal to the number of days simulated error: minshades must be a vector with a length equal to the number of days simulated

I have also used micro_ncep to analyse a full calendar year at the same location, which worked with default settings, but resulted in the same error when the scenario was changed.

Thank you for your help,

Shane

